  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 138 PM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nPersistence forecast for the next several days, and most of the\nnext week as the surface and lower levels of the atmosphere \nremain mostly under high pressure with ridging trying to build in \nfrom the west further up in the atmosphere. \n\nThis will lead to continued pleasant weather days with mostly clear \nskies, light winds, and temperatures right around seasonal normals. \nHave made a few tweaks to dew points and included patchy fog in the \nriver valleys as we've seen the past several mornings... But \notherwise this is a low impacts forecast for the southern \nAppalachians and eastern Tennessee Valley.\n\nIncreased clouds could move in next week as a trough swings through \nto our north, but as of this writing no precipitation is\nanticipated.",
